      "side": 1,
      "message": "It seems like `cuttoff_timeout` is not a time value but actually a number of polling iterations and should be called something like `cutoff_polling_iterations`.\n\nAnother way of doing it that seems a bit more expressive to me would be to compute the timeout timestamp with `get_time()` in `battery_cutoff_start` and then poll `timestamp_expired` in this function. Then you wouldn\u0027t have to maintain a relationship between `CONFIG_BATTERY_CUTOFF_TIMEOUT_MSEC` and `cutoff_poll_msec`, and you could get rid of some of your global variables.",
      "revId": "d2e9b1de09927449f45ee02c95d2014ad4dcfb42",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
